{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Sets a function to be called at regular intervals, with ","type":"text"},{"code":"priority","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/timeoutaddsecondsfull(priority:interval:function:data:notify:)"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"timeoutAddSecondsFull","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"priority","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"interval","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"function","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GSourceFunc","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@GSourceFunc"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"data","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gpointer","text":"gpointer"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"notify","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"GDestroyNotify","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@GDestroyNotify"},{"text":"? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The function is called repeatedly until it returns [const","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/sourceRemove"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"at which point the timeout is automatically destroyed and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the function will not be called again."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Unlike [func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.timeout_add"},{"type":"text","text":"], this function operates at whole second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"granularity. The initial starting point of the timer is determined by the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"implementation and the implementation is expected to group multiple timers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"together so that they fire all at the same time. To allow this grouping,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"interval"},{"text":" to the first timer is rounded and can deviate up to one second","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"from the specified interval. Subsequent timer iterations will generally run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"at the specified interval."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that timeout functions may be delayed, due to the processing of other"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"event sources. Thus they should not be relied on for precise timing."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"After each call to the timeout function, the time of the next"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"timeout is recalculated based on the current time and the given ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"interval"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"identifier":"main-loop.html#memory-management-of-sources","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for details","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on how to handle the return value and memory management of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"data"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you want timing more precise than whole seconds, use"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[func","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.timeout_add","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The grouping of timers to fire at the same time results in a more power"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and CPU efficient behavior so if your timer is in multiples of seconds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and you don’t require the first timer exactly one second from now, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use of [func","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.timeout_add_seconds","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] is preferred over"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.timeout_add"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This internally creates a main loop source using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.timeout_source_new_seconds"},{"type":"text","text":"] and attaches it to the main loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"context using [method","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.Source.attach","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]. You can do these steps manually"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"if you need greater control."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is safe to call this function from any thread."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The interval given is in terms of monotonic time, not wall clock"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time. See [func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.get_monotonic_time"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"met